## ---- Build output ----
[Bb]in/
[Oo]bj/
[Oo]ut/
[Ll]og/
[Ll]ogs/
*.log

## ---- Prebuilt client artifacts (WPF/Xamarin build output; never committed) ----
## Installer output and prebuilt client binaries are build artifacts, not source,
## and are never committed. The patterns below are kept in every repo in the set so
## that a client binary cannot be added by accident in one of them.
pc/Febris_PC_Installer/[Rr]elease/
*.msi
*.apk
*.aab
*.ipa

## The ffmpeg binary the screen recorder shells out to. It is a build/release input, fetched
## with pc/tools/fetch-ffmpeg.ps1 and copied beside the executable by the csproj, never committed
## (it is a large third-party GPL binary). Air-gapped builds supply it with -Path.
pc/tools/ffmpeg/

## ---- IDE / tooling ----
.vs/
.idea/
.vscode/
*.user
*.suo
*.userprefs
*_i.c
*.rsuser

## ---- Secrets & local config ----
## v4 principle: NO secrets in the repo. Real values come from environment
## variables, user-secrets, or a secret manager. Only *.template / *.example
## config is tracked.
appsettings.Development.json
appsettings.Staging.json
appsettings.*.local.json
appsettings.Local.json
secrets.json
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pfx
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
## Keystore formats. tools/status.sh has always used *.jks and *.keystore as its SIGN-1
## tripwire, so the project already treated those two as the formats that must never be
## tracked, yet neither was ignored here until 2026-08-31. The real signing keystore is a
## .p12 and lives off-tree, so nothing was ever exposed, but a .jks or .keystore dropped in
## the tree was stageable with no guard at any layer. .bks is the legacy Android Bouncy
## Castle form and carries the same material.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.bks
*.pubxml

## ASP.NET DataProtection key rings. AppKeys:KeyRingPath is the RELATIVE path "keys" in
## the enduser api and portal, so running either app from a clone mints an UNENCRYPTED
## master key beside the binaries. On 2026-08-29 a broad `git add` swept one into the
## public node repo. The *.key rule above does NOT cover it: a key ring is an XML file
## named key-<guid>.xml, not a .key file. Both forms are listed because the ring
## directory and a loose ring file each carry the same material.
## The directory rule is anchored to a path component named EXACTLY "keys". Do not
## loosen it to a substring match such as *keys*: the tracked vendored asset
## wwwroot/gentelella-master/vendors/jquery.hotkeys/ would be swallowed by that.
keys/
key-*.xml

## ---- OS ----
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

## ---- Python ----
## The repo is .NET, but tests/mutation/run-mutations.py is Python, and running it
## leaves bytecode beside itself.
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

## The 149.5 MB Default_video.mp4 lived here and exceeded GitHub's 100 MB hard
## limit, blocking the public push. Its only consumers were broken fallbacks.
enduser/FebrisEndUserPortal/wwwroot/images/DefaultMedia/*.mp4
simulationintegration/FebrisCpp/packages/
simulationintegration/FebrisCpp/x64/
simulationintegration/FebrisCpp/Febris.C.*/
simulationintegration/parity/out/
simulationintegration/parity/probe/build/
simulationintegration/parity/probe-abi/build/
